From 7f9beec9ddf34b12dc19d3c84958b39439bc398d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(terminal): isolate Docker storage by conversation

Keep Hermes' existing Docker backend and CLI contract, but add the two pieces
needed by a remote, least-privilege container engine:

* a conversation environment scope instead of the upstream global container;
* engine-owned named volumes instead of gateway-side bind paths.

Support-file mounts are independently suppressible because their source paths
belong to the gateway filesystem and are neither meaningful nor safe when the
Docker API is served by a different Unix account.
